---
description: Pytest isolation and behavior coverage for backend tests
globs: backend/tests/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Use pytest. Prefer the lowest test that proves the behavior:

- Unit: service rules, with the repository mocked.
- Integration: repository and database behavior on sqlite in-memory or a
  disposable test Postgres.
- API: validation, auth, and the response contract.

Test behavior and failure paths. Do not add a test per tiny function when
an existing higher-level test already covers it. Add a regression test for
a bug fix when practical.

Tests must be deterministic. Use fixtures, fakes, or mocks. Do not depend
on machine state, test order, production databases, real external APIs,
real model providers, or real credentials.

Do not mock the unit under test. Do not delete or weaken a test to make an
implementation pass.
